@using Sandbox
@using Sandbox.UI
@using System.Linq
@using Terryball
@inherits PanelComponent

@*
	The how-to-play screen. Walking up to the HELP podium on the settee and pressing E opens this
	(TerryAvatar runs the engage / cursor-free, like the other podiums). Read-only text —
	joining/starting at the lane controls (incl. the Throw-style and ball-crane toggles), the ball
	designer, and the two bowling styles (FREE ride / guided AIM). Pointer-events: none except the
	modal, like LaneControls/BallDesigner.
*@

<root style="position: absolute; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none;
             font-family: Poppins, sans-serif; color: white;">
	@{
		var me = LocalAvatar;
	}

	@if ( me is not null )
	{
		@* Walk-up prompt: near the help podium but not engaged yet. *@
		@if ( me.NearHelp && !me.HelpOpen )
		{
			<div style="position: absolute; bottom: 64px; left: 0px; right: 0px;
			            flex-direction: row; justify-content: center;">
				<div style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; padding: 10px 24px; border-radius: 10px;
				            background-color: rgba(8,10,16,0.54);
				            border-width: 1px; border-color: rgba(241,196,15,0.4);">
					Press <span style="color: #f1c40f; font-weight: 800;">E</span> — How To Play
				</div>
			</div>
		}

		@if ( me.HelpOpen )
		{
			<div style="position: absolute; width: 100%; height: 100%;
			            flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
				<div style="pointer-events: all; flex-direction: column; width: 1000px;
				            padding: 30px 38px; border-radius: 18px; background-color: rgba(8,10,16,0.80);
				            border-width: 2px; border-color: rgba(241,196,15,0.5);">

					<div style="flex-direction: row; font-size: 32px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 18px;">
						<div>HOW TO&nbsp;</div>
						<div style="color: #f1c40f;">PLAY</div>
					</div>

					<div style="font-size: 17px; font-weight: 800; color: #5aa0e6; margin-bottom: 6px;">1 — JOIN &amp; START (the LANE podium)</div>
					<div style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); margin-bottom: 16px;">
						Walk up to the LANE podium and press E to open the lane controls. Hit JOIN to get on the
						roster (LEAVE to drop back out); press START when everyone's in. Two lane-wide settings sit
						up top — the Throw style (FREE or AIM, see step 3) and the Ball Crane (ON, the crane flies
						out to scoop each bowler into the ball; OFF, you're placed straight in). Pick both in the
						lobby before you press START.
					</div>

					<div style="font-size: 17px; font-weight: 800; color: #b07de6; margin-bottom: 6px;">2 — DESIGN YOUR BALL (the BALL podium)</div>
					<div style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); margin-bottom: 16px;">
						Press E at the BALL podium to open the ball designer. Pick a pattern (Half &amp; Half,
						Polkadot, Cubes, Galaxy) and tune the two colour sliders — the spinning preview shows
						exactly what you'll get. Your look saves automatically when you leave and everyone sees
						it on the ball when you're up.
					</div>

					<div style="font-size: 17px; font-weight: 800; color: #2ecc71; margin-bottom: 6px;">3 — BOWL!</div>
					@* NOTE: no inline <span>s here — s&box panels lay children out as flex items, not inline
					   text flow, so mixed spans shatter the paragraph into columns. Plain text lines only. *@
					<div style="flex-direction: column; margin-bottom: 20px;">
						<div style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); margin-bottom: 8px;">
							Your turn plays one of two ways, set by the Throw toggle at the LANE podium. Knock down all ten!
						</div>
						<div style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #6fd3ff; margin-bottom: 2px;">FREE — ride the ball</div>
						<div style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); margin-bottom: 8px;">
							You ride INSIDE the ball. Steer with WASD (mouse to look) — full control all the way down
							the approach, right up to the blue THROW line. Crossing it commits the throw and hands the
							ball to physics, so line it up and give it some pace.
						</div>
						<div style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #b07de6; margin-bottom: 2px;">AIM — guided throw</div>
						<div style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); margin-bottom: 8px;">
							The ball parks behind the foul line and you line the shot up in four steps — LINE, AIM,
							POWER, SPIN. Slide each left/right with the mouse (or A/D) and lock it with click or Space;
							right-click (or Backspace) steps back to redo one. POWER and SPIN have a sweet spot around
							80% — maxing them out overcooks the shot. The curved aim arrow previews the hook: the ball
							skids straight through the oiled front of the lane, then breaks toward the pocket over the
							dry back end, so spin curves it LATE instead of flinging it off the line.
						</div>
						<div style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85);">
							G bails you out of the ball; R respawns you on the settee if you get stuck walking around.
						</div>
					</div>

					@* The SETTINGS pedestal is on the spawn concourse, not the settee, so it needs saying —
					   a player who teleports straight to a lane never walks past it. *@
					<div style="font-size: 17px; font-weight: 800; color: #f1c40f; margin-bottom: 6px;">4 — MAKE IT YOURS (the SETTINGS pedestal)</div>
					<div style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); margin-bottom: 16px;">
						Back at the spawn concourse, press E at the SETTINGS pedestal for the theme colour every
						panel in the alley is tinted from, how bright the sky over it is, and how far away you can
						hear other players talk. All three are yours alone — saved on this machine, and nobody
						else's alley changes.
					</div>

					<div style="font-size: 17px; font-weight: 800; color: #f1c40f; margin-bottom: 6px;">5 — INVITE YOUR FRIENDS!</div>
					<div style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); margin-bottom: 10px;">
						Terryball is multiplayer — up to 16 players share the alley, take turns on the roster and
						watch each other bowl. Invite friends through the Steam overlay,
						and come hang out on the Discord — the invite is on the MORE podium out on the concourse,
						next to the teleporter.
					</div>

					<div style="flex-direction: row;">
						<div style="flex-grow: 1;"></div>
						<div style="pointer-events: all; padding: 12px 28px; border-radius: 9px;
						            font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer;
						            background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.12);"
						     onclick=@CloseHelp>
							CLOSE (E)
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		}
	}
</root>

@code
{
	private TerryAvatar LocalAvatar =>
		Scene?.GetAllComponents<TerryAvatar>().FirstOrDefault( a => a.IsValid() && !a.IsProxy );

	private void CloseHelp() => LocalAvatar?.RequestCloseHelp();

	protected override int BuildHash()
	{
		var me = LocalAvatar;
		return System.HashCode.Combine( me?.NearHelp, me?.HelpOpen );
	}
}
